#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:1
msgid "Class: RetryAgent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:3
msgid "Extends: `undici.Dispatcher`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:5
msgid ""
"A `undici.Dispatcher` that allows to automatically retry a request. Wraps"
" a `undici.RetryHandler`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:8
msgid "`new RetryAgent(dispatcher, [options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:10
msgid "Arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:12
msgid "**dispatcher** `undici.Dispatcher` (required) - the dispatcher to wrap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:13
msgid "**options** `RetryHandlerOptions` (optional) - the options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:15
msgid "Returns: `ProxyAgent`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:17
msgid "Parameter: `RetryHandlerOptions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:19
msgid ""
"**throwOnError** `boolean` (optional) - Disable to prevent throwing error"
" on last retry attept, useful if you need the body on errors from server "
"or if you have custom error handler. Default: `true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:20
msgid ""
"**retry** `(err: Error, context: RetryContext, callback: (err?: Error | "
"null) => void) => void` (optional) - Function to be called after every "
"retry. It should pass error if no more retries should be performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:21
msgid ""
"**maxRetries** `number` (optional) - Maximum number of retries. Default: "
"`5`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:22
msgid ""
"**maxTimeout** `number` (optional) - Maximum number of milliseconds to "
"wait before retrying. Default: `30000` (30 seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:23
msgid ""
"**minTimeout** `number` (optional) - Minimum number of milliseconds to "
"wait before retrying. Default: `500` (half a second)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:24
msgid ""
"**timeoutFactor** `number` (optional) - Factor to multiply the timeout by"
" for each retry attempt. Default: `2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:25
msgid ""
"**retryAfter** `boolean` (optional) - It enables automatic retry after "
"the `Retry-After` header is received. Default: `true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:27
msgid ""
"**methods** `string[]` (optional) - Array of HTTP methods to retry. "
"Default: `['GET', 'PUT', 'HEAD', 'OPTIONS', 'DELETE']`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:28
msgid ""
"**statusCodes** `number[]` (optional) - Array of HTTP status codes to "
"retry. Default: `[429, 500, 502, 503, 504]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:29
msgid ""
"**errorCodes** `string[]` (optional) - Array of Error codes to retry. "
"Default: `['ECONNRESET', 'ECONNREFUSED', 'ENOTFOUND', "
"'ENETDOWN','ENETUNREACH', 'EHOSTDOWN', 'UND_ERR_SOCKET']`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:31
msgid "**`RetryContext`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:33
msgid "`state`: `RetryState` - Current retry state. It can be mutated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_RetryAgent.md:34
msgid ""
"`opts`: `Dispatch.DispatchOptions & RetryOptions` - Options passed to the"
" retry handler."
msgstr ""

